        "original_id": "bd285172-ecbb-56ec-bd6e-97bcdbdd14c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl, 2009 Big East Conference football season\n- Teams: Rutgers Scarlet Knights, UCF, Big East football members\n- People: Mohamed Sanu\n- Places: Tropicana Field, St. Petersburg, Florida\n\nFacts:\n- The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl presented by Beef 'O' Brady's was formerly known as the St. Petersburg Bowl and was the second edition of the college football bowl game.\n- The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl was played at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Florida.\n- The Big East Conference had eight football members in 2009: Cincinnati, Connecticut, Louisville, Pittsburgh, Rutgers, South Florida, Syracuse, and West Virginia.\n- The 2009 Rutgers Scarlet Knights football team finished 9–4 overall and 3–4 in Big East play.\n- The 2009 Rutgers Scarlet Knights football team won the St. Petersburg Bowl 45–24 over UCF.\n- In the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl, Rutgers defeated UCF 45–24.\n- In the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl, Mohamed Sanu was the game's MVP.\n- In the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl, Mohamed Sanu caught 4 passes for 97 yards and a touchdown and rushed 14 times for 47 yards and two touchdowns.\n- Mohamed Sanu Sr., born August 22, 1989, is an American football wide receiver for the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
